  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Distributed Transaction Problems",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Distributed Transaction Problems",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why ACID stops at the service",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One business operation spans ==several services==",
                "Each service owns its **own database**",
                "No single ACID transaction can cover all of them"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Two-phase commit (2PC)",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Prepare",
                    "note": "coordinator asks all",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Votes",
                    "note": "each says yes or no",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Commit or abort",
                    "note": "all or nothing",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "2PC is ==blocking==",
                "Coordinator crash: participants {red:hold locks} until it returns"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Dual writes and CAP",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Dual write==: DB update and broker publish are two steps",
                "Crash between them: DB and broker are **out of sync**",
                "Network partition: choose {blue:consistency} or {green:availability}",
                "Most microservices choose ==availability=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Retries need idempotency",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "curl -X POST /charges \\",
                "  -H \"Idempotency-Key: order-42-charge\""
              ],
              "note": "server stores the key and replays the first result"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Retry without a key",
              "text": "A retry repeats the side effect, such as a ==double charge==. Give every step an **idempotency key**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Saga Pattern: Choreography vs Orchestration",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Saga Pattern: Choreography vs Orchestration",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a saga is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Saga== = sequence of **local transactions**, one per service",
                "Each step has a ==compensating transaction==",
                "If a later step fails, compensations **semantically undo** the earlier ones"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Choreography vs orchestration",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Choreography",
                "Orchestration"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Control",
                  "services react to **events**",
                  "central ==orchestrator== sends commands"
                ],
                [
                  "State",
                  "spread across services",
                  "tracked by orchestrator"
                ],
                [
                  "Strength",
                  "{green:loosely coupled}",
                  "{green:easy to follow}"
                ],
                [
                  "Weakness",
                  "{red:hard to trace}, cyclic dependencies",
                  "{red:coupling point}, keep it thin"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: payment fails",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Reserve stock",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Charge payment",
                    "sub": "fails",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Release stock",
                    "sub": "compensate 1",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cancel order",
                    "sub": "compensate 2",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sagas are ==not isolated==: concurrent sagas see intermediate state",
                "Counter with **semantic locks**, a `PENDING` status, or commutative updates",
                "Compensations must be ==idempotent== and retryable",
                "Irreversible actions, like a sent email, cannot be undone"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Undo in reverse",
              "text": "Run compensations in ==reverse order==. A saga never rolls back; it compensates forward."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Outbox Pattern",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Outbox Pattern",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Outbox",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Write the ==business row== and an ==outbox event row== in the **same local DB transaction**",
                "Both commit or both roll back, so the {green:dual-write problem} is gone",
                "Publishing to the broker happens later, from the outbox table"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "One DB transaction",
                    "sub": "order row + outbox row",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Relay",
                    "sub": "poll or CDC",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "sub": "publish event",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Mark sent",
                    "sub": "after publish",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Relay and Delivery",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Polling",
                "CDC (log tailing)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "How",
                  "Query unsent rows on a timer",
                  "Read the DB log, e.g. **Debezium**"
                ],
                [
                  "Latency",
                  "Higher",
                  "{green:Lower}"
                ],
                [
                  "DB load",
                  "Extra query load",
                  "{green:None}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Relay can crash ==after publish, before marking sent==",
                "So delivery is **at-least-once**: duplicates happen",
                "Consumers must be ==idempotent=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Inbox and Gotchas",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Inbox pattern",
              "items": [
                "Consumer stores processed ==message IDs== in a table",
                "Skip the message if its ID is already there",
                "Insert the ID in the {purple:same transaction} as its own update"
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Gotchas",
              "text": "Key messages on the ==aggregate ID== to keep order per aggregate. **Purge** sent outbox rows or the table grows forever."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CQRS and Event Sourcing",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CQRS and Event Sourcing",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. CQRS",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Write model}: ==commands== change state",
                "{green:Read model}: ==queries== over denormalized views",
                "Each is **scaled and stored** independently",
                "Projections consume write-side events, so reads ==lag== writes: **eventually consistent**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Command",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Write model",
                    "sub": "emits event",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Projection",
                    "sub": "lag here",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Read model",
                    "sub": "query view",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Event Sourcing",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Append-only log== of **immutable** events is the source of truth",
                "State = ==fold (replay)== of one aggregate's events",
                "==Snapshot== every N events: no full replay"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Load snapshot",
                    "note": "state at event N",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Replay newer events",
                    "note": "N+1 onward",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Current state",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Together and Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CQRS",
                "Event sourcing"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Without the other?",
                  "{green:Yes}",
                  "Rarely"
                ],
                [
                  "Needs for queries",
                  "Nothing",
                  "Almost always ==CQRS=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Events never change",
              "text": "Fix a mistake with a ==compensating event==. Handle schema changes by **versioning** or ==upcasting== old events."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Eventual Consistency in Practice",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Eventual Consistency in Practice",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Eventual Consistency",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No new updates → all replicas and read models ==converge== to the same value",
                "Reads in between may be {red:stale}",
                "Gap = replication or {blue:projection lag}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Living With It",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Read-your-writes==: send that user's reads to the **primary**",
                "Or wait until the projection reaches the write's ==version==",
                "At-least-once delivery → **duplicates are normal**",
                "Idempotent consumer: check a ==dedupe key== first"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "INSERT INTO inbox(msg_id) VALUES ($1)",
                "  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;",
                "-- 0 rows inserted: duplicate, skip",
                "UPDATE ...; COMMIT;"
              ],
              "note": "dedupe insert and the update share one transaction"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choose the Pattern",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Scope",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "One service's DB",
                  "**Strong** consistency (local ACID)"
                ],
                [
                  "Across services",
                  "==Saga=="
                ],
                [
                  "Few trusted XA resources",
                  "`2PC`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not for simple CRUD",
              "text": "Sagas, CQRS and event sourcing each add ==operational cost==. Use them only where the business needs them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Distributed Consistency Patterns",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Distributed Consistency Patterns",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Problem to pattern",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Problem",
                "Pattern"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Cross-service atomicity",
                  "==Saga=="
                ],
                [
                  "DB plus broker write",
                  "==Outbox=="
                ],
                [
                  "Read/write scaling",
                  "==CQRS=="
                ],
                [
                  "Full audit and replay",
                  "==Event sourcing=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Saga choice and delivery",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Choreography}: 2-4 simple steps",
                "{blue:Orchestration}: complex or branching flows",
                "==At-least-once== delivery + idempotent consumers = **effectively-once**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Compensation rule",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Undo in ==reverse order==",
                "Make every undo ==idempotent==",
                "Never rely on rollback"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Payment fails",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Release stock",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cancel order",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Checklist",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Idempotency key== on every step",
                "==Outbox row== in the same transaction",
                "==Versioned== events",
                "==Projection lag== monitoring"
              ],
              "style": "checkbox"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A service commits an order row, then crashes before publishing OrderCreated to the broker. What state is the system in, and what fixes it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Order exists, but no one hears about it: the DB and broker are out of sync.",
                "Fix: write an outbox row in the same transaction; a relay publishes it later."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "The outbox relay publishes a row, then crashes before marking it sent. What happens on restart?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The row is published again: delivery is at-least-once.",
                "Consumers must dedupe by message ID, ideally in the same transaction as their update."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Saga: reserve stock, charge payment, ship. Shipping fails. What runs, in what order?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Refund payment, then release stock, then cancel order: reverse order.",
                "Each compensation must be idempotent, since it may be retried."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
